.TH FL-REMOTE 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.4" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-remote \- VNC and RDP remote desktop viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-remote\fR [vnc://\fIhost\fR[:\fIport\fR] | rdp://[\fIuser\fR@]\fIhost\fR[:\fIport\fR] | \fIhost\fR[:\fIport\fR]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Keeps a list of connections to other computers. VNC connections open in a
window of their own (fl-remote speaks the RFB protocol itself: no password
or a VNC password; the screen scales to the window): the mouse and the
keyboard go to the remote computer, its clipboard text comes here, and
\fBF8\fR opens a menu to scale, send the clipboard, send Ctrl+Alt+Delete or
disconnect. RDP connections (Windows) open in the FreeRDP client
(\fBwlfreerdp\fR, \fBsdl-freerdp\fR or \fBxfreerdp\fR), which must be
installed. Passwords are asked for and never saved.
.SH FILES
\fI~/.config/fldesktop/remote.ini\fR: the saved connections.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBxfreerdp\fR(1), \fBwayvnc\fR(1)
